Note-Taking App 
Midterm assignment by Mahyar Naeimi
A full-stack Note-Taking App built with Node.js, Express, MongoDB, and EJS.
This project demonstrates understanding of server-side JavaScript, RESTful API creation, authentication (local & Google OAuth), and integration with a front-end interface.

Features
User authentication:

Local login & registration (email + password)

Google OAuth 2.0 login with Passport

CRUD operations for notes:

Create, read, update, and delete personal notes

Notes are private to each logged-in user

Authentication & session handling with express-session and MongoDB store

Passwords are securely hashed with bcryptjs

Server-side validation and error handling

Simple EJS + TailwindCSS front-end for login, registration, and note management

RESTful API endpoints for note management






Project Structure
Note_Taking_App/
│
├── config/
│   └── passport.js        # Google OAuth + Passport config
│
├── middlewares/
│   ├── asyncHandler.js    # Async error handling
│   ├── auth.js            # Authentication middleware
│   └── error.js           # Global error handlers
│
├── models/
│   ├── note.js            # Note schema
│   └── user.js            # User schema
│
├── routes/
│   ├── auth.js            # Auth routes (login, register, Google OAuth)
│   └── post.js            # Notes CRUD routes
│
├── views/
│   ├── index.ejs          # Login page
│   ├── register.ejs       # Register page
│   ├── forgot-password.ejs# Forgot password page
│   └── ...                # Shared layouts
│
├── public/                # Static assets (CSS, images, favicon)
│
├── seed.js                # DB seeder (test user + notes)
├── app.js                 # Main Express server
├── package.json
└── README.md



Installation & Setup
1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/Mahyarnaeimi/Note-taking-app
cd note-taking-app

2. Install dependencies
npm install nodemon

3. Create .env file
PORT=3500
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/note_taker
SESSION_SECRET=your-secret-key
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3500/auth/google/callback

4. Seed the database (optional)
Creates a test user and sample notes.
npm run seed

5. Run the server
npm run dev

Server will be running at:
 http://localhost:3500


Authentication
Local Login/Register


/auth/register → register with email & password


/auth/login → login with email & password


Google Login


/auth/google → login with Google account


Session & Logout


Sessions stored in MongoDB via connect-mongo


/auth/logout → logout user



API Endpoints
All note routes require authentication (ensureAuth middleware).
Method
Endpoint
Description
GET
/posts/
Get all notes (for user)
POST
/posts/
Create a new note
GET
/posts/:id
Get a single note by ID
PUT
/posts/:id
Update a note (owner only)
DELETE
/posts/:id
Delete a note (owner only)



Validation & Error Handling
Invalid login credentials redirect with error message


Unauthorized access → 401 Unauthorized

Accessing another user’s note → 403 Forbidden

Non-existing routes → custom 404.html

Front-End (EJS + TailwindCSS)
index.ejs → login form & error handling

register.ejs → register new user

forgot-password.ejs → password reset request

TailwindCSS used for responsive design

Technologies Used
Node.js + Express – server & routing

MongoDB + Mongoose – database & models

Passport.js – authentication (local + Google OAuth 2.0)

express-session + connect-mongo – session handling

bcryptjs – password hashing

EJS – templating engine

TailwindCSS – UI styling

morgan – request logging

Notes.

Passwords should always be hashed before storing in DB.

Use HTTPS + secure cookie flags in production.



